<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Nassau-Diez</h1><p class="st-meta">1606 CE – 1806 CE · capital Diez</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nassau territory on the Lahn whose counts, as hereditary stadtholders of Friesland, became the House of Orange-Nassau that rules the Netherlands today.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diez">Diez</a> arose in the 1606 partition of the lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-count-of-nassau-dillenburg">John VI of Nassau-Dillenburg</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-casimir-i-count-of-nassau-dietz">Ernst Casimir</a> received Diez on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahn">Lahn</a>. Ernst Casimir served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> as a general and became stadtholder of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-frisia">Friesland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groningen">Groningen</a>, beginning his line's long connection with the northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The German lands were small and governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diez">Diez</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oranienstein-palace">Oranienstein</a> palace, while the counts spent their careers in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, where they held the Frisian stadtholdership hereditarily. They were raised to princes of the Empire in 1654. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-william-friso">John William Friso</a> inherited part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-england">William III</a>'s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-orange">Orange</a> claims in 1702, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-prince-of-orange">William IV</a> united all Nassau-Ottonian lands by 1743.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-prince-of-orange">William IV</a> became stadtholder of all the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">United Provinces</a> in 1747. In 1806 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> confiscated the German lands, which went to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grand-duchy-of-berg">Grand Duchy of Berg</a>, and after 1815 they passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-nassau">Duchy of Nassau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. William IV's grandson became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-the-netherlands">King William I of the Netherlands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1606 CE – 1806 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.66%;width:3.98%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1606 CE – 1806 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Diez</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ernst Casimir, John William Friso, William IV</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Calvinism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nassau-Diez, Nassau-Orange</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1706&amp;focus=principality-of-nassau-diez" aria-label="Principality of Nassau-Diez on the atlas"><svg class="